I just lost my best game to date to a minotaur on the castle level.  I had
just come down the stairs to level 28, feeling pretty good.  My hit points
were at maximum (114 -- I was a level 13 Samurai).  I fell down the stairs,
and landed at the feet (hooves?) of a very mean-looking 'H'.  My first idea
was to teleport away, but a mysterious force prevented that.  (I assume that
means I was on the castle level.)  Then I hit him with a wand of fire.  That
just made him angry, and he stomped on me some more.  A hit with Mjollnir, then
prayer, then a potion of sickness, another hit with Mojo, etc.  The dude would
not die.  But I did.

Questions: (no, I wasn't just posting this for sympathy).  What should I have
done?  I was operating under the (possibly false) assumption that he would have
followed me up the stairs.  Should I have dropped some junk and headed up?
Would another weapon have done better (I also had on my person Stormbringer
[gotten from a magic lamp] and Excalibur)?  Maybe the wand of fire again?  Was
I simply not ready for this?

Any thoughts would be appreciated; this was only my second time at the castle
level.  BTW, I did eliminate the minotaur on level 27, but had a cockatrice
corpse with me at the time....  The one on level 26, I simply avoided.
